<title>SOUTH KOREA: Maxtor mulls moving S.Korean lines to Singapore.</title>
<headline>Maxtor mulls moving S.Korean lines to Singapore.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maxtor Corp, a unit of Hyundai Electronics Industries Co's U.S. subsidiary, is considering moving its hard disk drive production lines in South Korea to Singapore, a Hyundai Electronics spokesman said on Friday.</p>
<p>He said Maxtor had requested Hyundai Electronics, a unit of the Hyundai Group, to allow the relocation which is aimed at simplifying its production management.</p>
<p>&quot;A final decision will be made later, most possibly towards the end of this year,&quot; said the spokesman.</p>
<p>Maxtor, a specialised maker of computer hard disk drives, already operates production lines in Singapore and Thailand.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
